  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Radius of circular path of charged particle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>q</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>m</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;moving with velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>v</mi></mfenced></math> in magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>"
